    "text": "Reduction of Alkynes"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "7d623ee1-3ece-428f-8e7f-413036d2b3f5"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00107:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00107:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Acetylene reacts with hydrogen and catalyst to form ethene. Ethene reacts with hydrogen and catalyst to form ethane. The standard enthalpy of hydrogen for both reactions is given."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_09_05_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00107:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00107:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The reaction shows 4-octyne reacting with hydrogen and Lindlar's catalyst to give cis-4-octene. This reacts with hydrogen, and palladium catalyst to form octane. Quinoline is also used in the process."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_09_05_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00107:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00107:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "An alkyne reacts with hydrogen and Lindlar catalyst to give 7-cis-retinol (7-cis-vitamin A; vitamin A has a trans double bond at C7)."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_09_05_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00107:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00107:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "The figure shows 5-decyne reacting with lithium and ammonia to form trans-5-decene (78%)."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_09_05_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00107:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00107:caption:fig-00005-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00107:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "The figure shows the mechanism of reduction of an alkyne in the presence of lithium and ammonium in four steps to give a trans alkene."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_09_05_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
